{"title":"Career Roadmap · Ayush Assistant","role":"Ayush Assistant","summary":"An Ayush Assistant supports the delivery of healthcare services within AYUSH systems, including Ayurveda, Yoga & Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homoeopathy, depending on the institution and role.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Ayurveda Allied (Panchakarma Technician / Ayurveda Pharmacy)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Ayush Assistant supports the delivery of healthcare services within AYUSH systems, including Ayurveda, Yoga & Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homoeopathy, depending on the institution and role."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is generally support-oriented rather than an independent physician role. Depending on the employer and qualification, responsibilities can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Supporting AYUSH practitioners"},{"text":"Patient registration and coordination"},{"text":"Preparing treatment areas"},{"text":"Assisting with prescribed therapies"},{"text":"Panchakarma-related support"},{"text":"Maintaining treatment equipment"},{"text":"Basic patient observation"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Pharmacy/store support"},{"text":"Hygiene and infection-control procedures"},{"text":"Appointment coordination"},{"text":"Patient education within authorized scope"},{"text":"Maintaining treatment records"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“AYUSH Assistant” is a broad job title and can mean different things across government AYUSH facilities, hospitals, wellness centres and private institutions. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be treated as qualifying for every AYUSH Assistant post. Eligibility depends on the specific employer, job notification, recognized qualification and scope of practice."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"t